\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.   What shall I render to praise you\cf0 
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Master of Power, and Might?
\par Give to me, thy Holy Spirit,
\par that my word shall be so pleased!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And the sign of Thy love to me
\par and thy grace be over my mind.
\par God Almighty, King of Kings
\par We give You thanks and praise Thee!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When 'er I remember my sins
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 that You paid for so dearly,
\par That makes me to feel so shameful
\par that You still keep me alive,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par and You care for me a poor man,
\par and You  are so meek for my sake
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   God Almighty, King of Kings\'85.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   Master, Thou keep on follow me
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0    deliver me from hell fire;
\par     And the day that I with sinners
\par    looked for all those rotting things
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Thou beckon me to look for you,
\par  Thy Kingdom and Thy righteousness
\par  God Almighty, King of Kings....
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And sometimes you want to come with
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj  Love to all of your children;
\par  and sometimes too, through some pains \tab 
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj you would want us to draw so near
\par  to make us learn from your good deeds
\par  and to make us follow your words
\par  God Almighty, King of Kings\'85\'85
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Father, Thou revealed your mercies
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0  And your love to your children
\par  Jesus, it is your love and grace
\par  that gives me my happyness.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And Thy Holy Spirit is still
\par   keeping directing to Heaven
\par  By Thy grace if I may get there,
\par \pard      I'll give you praise for ever.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

